==Hebrew==

===Etymology===
{{he-rootbox|י־ד־ד}}
Related to {{cog|ar|وَدِيد||friendly, beloved}} and {{cog|uga|𐎊𐎄||beloved}} (according to Even Shoshan dictionary).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|he|/jɔːˈðiːð/ [jɔːˈðiːð]|a=Tiberian Hebrew}}
* {{IPA|he|/jɔˈðið/ [jɔːˈðiːð]|a=Yemenite Hebrew}}
* {{IPA|he|/jaˈdid/|a=Modern Israeli}}

===Noun===
{{he-noun|wv=יָדִיד|tr=yadíd|g=m|cons=יְדִיד|pl=יְדִידִים|plcons=יְדִידֵי|f=יְדִידָה|pat=קָטִיל}}

# A (male) [[friend]].
# {{lb|he|hbo}} [[darling]], [[beloved]]

====Usage notes====
* While the synonym {{m|he|חָבֵר|tr=khavér}} is more common in Modern Hebrew, it is ambiguous between a platonic friend and a romantic one. Therefore, to avoid this ambiguity, {{m|he|יָדִיד}} may be used, or [[w:contrastive focus reduplication|contrastive focus reduplication]] may be used as in the question {{l|he||חבר חבר או רק חבר?|tr=''khavér'' khavér o rak khavér?|gloss=boyfriend-friend or just friend?}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|friend}} {{l|he|חָבֵר|tr=khavér|g=m}}

